Aquaculture and wild aquatic foods (@farming-aquatic-foods: 0, is #trail, #contains @farming-aquaculture-cycle, #contains @oreochromis-niloticus, #contains @salmo-salar, #contains @penaeus-vannamei, #contains @prochilodus-lineatus, #contains @pseudoplatystoma-corruscans, #contains @farming-fish-identity, #contains @sardina-pilchardus) { r_0YEX298P6W6YXAHDZK8WEYWG7H
Several fish in Nutrients.lingua come from wild fisheries. A market name does not prove a species or make a fish a practical farm animal. Aquaculture examples below identify a possible production species explicitly; they do not relabel unspecified food samples.
